cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this scoped proof and the prior sources in its manuscript."
title: "Three independent third turns in six-dimensional kissing codes: a sharp 60-point rigidity threshold"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Yongxian
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-3864-3536"
version: 1.0.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/mxym/math"
abstract: "For unit six-dimensional kissing codes invariant under independent 120-degree rotations in three orthogonal planes, the exact maxima with zero, one, and two full-support orbits are 60, 57, and 72. Every code in this class of size greater than 60 has a unique E6 completion. There is one non-E6 60-point extremizer up to isometry. No unrestricted kissing number is asserted."
